    {
        "content": "<p><code>a + b</code> elaborates to <code>binop% HAdd.hAdd a b</code>, which I think usually wants everything to be homogeneous (see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=FBinopElab.elabBinOp#doc\">docs#FBinopElab.elabBinOp</a>)</p>",
        "id": 617536757,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787169119
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess a related question this is if this justifies defining <code>PFunctor.add</code> separate from the <code>HAdd</code> instance, or if the expected solution is to just write out <code>HAdd.hAdd</code> when the <code>binop%</code> parser doesn't work?</p>",
        "id": 617537781,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1787169335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Universe.20unification.20with.20.60HAdd.2EhAdd.60.20vs.2E.20.60.2B.60.20notation/near/617536757\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>which I think usually wants everything to be homogeneous</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>My hope was that the semantics were closer to \"tries homogenous first, then falls back to heterogenous\"</p>",
        "id": 617543986,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787171225
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perhaps <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"306601\">@Kyle Miller</span> has thoughts here</p>",
        "id": 617543997,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1787171230
    }
]